                              <div  class="col-xl-5 col-lg-5 col-md-6 col-12">
          <div class="_none mb-6 block block-layout-builder block-field-blocknodeplatformfield-description-formatted">
  
    
      <div class="content">
      
            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-description-formatted field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="tex2jax_process"><p>The Soil Moisture Active-Passive (SMAP) platform measures surface soil moisture and freeze-thaw state. These direct measurements improve our understanding of regional water cycles, ecosystem productivity, and processes that link the water, energy, and carbon cycles. Soil moisture information at high resolution enables improvements in weather, flood, and drought forecasts, and predictions of agricultural productivity and climate change.</p><p>SMAP measures surface soil conditions everywhere on Earth every two to three days, distinguishing between ground that is frozen or thawed. In ground that is not frozen or covered in water, SMAP measures how much water is in the top layer of soil. This data is used to produce global maps of soil moisture.</p></div></div>
      
    </div>
  </div>
<div class="_none block block-layout-builder block-field-blocknodeplatformfield-info-link">
  
    
      <div class="content">
      
            <div class="field field--name-field-info-link field--type-link field--label-hidden field__item">


<a href="https://smap.jpl.nasa.gov/"
      class="h5 text-decoration-none"
    >
      Learn more about SMAP
    <i class="hdsi hdsi-ui-arrow-line-right-circle-fill text-secondary ps-1 align-middle font-size-20"></i>
  </a>
</div>
      
    </div>
  </div>

